      <div type="clause" n="11">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 11</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="500–501" ed="#liebermann"/>Si ceo avient, que aucuns coupe le puing a l’auter u le pié, si lui rendrad demi were sulunc ceo qu’il est nez.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.18"/><pb n="500–501" ed="#liebermann"/>Si ço avent, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.14"/> alquen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.c"/> colpe le poin a altre u le pied, si li rendra demi were sulu[n]c<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.19"/> ceo qu’il<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.20"/> est nez<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.21"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="500–501" ed="#liebermann"/>De membrorum mutilacione. Si quis alteri uel manum uel pedem abscidit, dimidium were illi reddat iuxta statum conditionis sue.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="11" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="258" ed="#robertson"/>Si ceo avient que aucuns coupe le puing a l'auter u le pié, si lui rendrad demi were sulunc ceo qu'il est nez.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="500–501" ed="#liebermann"/>11. Wenn Folgendes vorkommt, dass jemand die Hand oder den Fuss dem anderen abhaut, so soll er ihm die Hälfte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_11.lnote.de.1"/> des, je nachdem jener geboren ist, [hohen] Wergelds zahlen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">11. If the following occurs, that someone cuts off the hand or the foot of another, then he shall pay him half of the wergild, [high] according as that man is born.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="259" ed="#robertson"/>If it happens that a man cuts off the hand or foot of another, he shall pay him (as compensation) half his wergeld according to his inherited rank.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 258–259 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 500–501, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">500</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">alquens <hi rend="italic">bessert BARTSCH</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">alquens emended by BARTSCH</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">500</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">500</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XIII. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XIII. I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">500</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">suluc <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">suluc I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">500</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">q’il <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> que il <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">q’il Io; que il Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_11.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">500</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mez <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mez Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_11.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Hand 9; Fuss 1—2; Wergeld 3. 4c. 5; bei anderen Germanen Brunner II 635</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Hand 9; Fuss 1—2; Wergeld 3. 4c. 5; among other Germanic peoples Brunner II 635</seg></note>
      </div>
